    \textbf{Skin disease calibration results (DermaMNIST).}
    \textbf{Left:} ECE-Hard (hatched) vs.\ ECE-Soft (solid) for all methods.
    TS and Platt (PS) achieve low hard ECE but exhibit a large calibration gap
    ($\Delta\approx 8$--$9$ pp) on soft labels, consistent with CIFAR-10H.
    Soft-label methods (SLTS, MCTS, HB-Soft, IR-Soft) substantially reduce
    ECE-Soft while maintaining competitive hard ECE.
    \textbf{Right:} ECE-Soft stratified by annotation entropy quartile.
    The calibration gap is largest in Q4 (high ambiguity), dominated by
    Mel$\leftrightarrow$NV confusions — the clinically most critical
    ambiguity in dermatology.
  }
  \label{fig:derm}
\end{figure}

