\section{Implementation Details}
\label{app:impl}

\paragraph{Model and fine-tuning.}
We use ResNet-50 with ImageNet-1k pretrained weights (PyTorch torchvision
\texttt{ResNet50\_Weights.IMAGENET1K\_V1}).  The final FC layer is replaced
with a random linear layer of shape $2048\times 10$.  Fine-tuning uses
AdamW with initial learning rate $10^{-4}$, weight decay $10^{-4}$, batch
size 128, and cosine learning rate annealing for 30 epochs.  Images are
resized to $224\times 224$ with standard ImageNet normalisation.

\paragraph{Calibration optimisation.}
TS, SLTS, and MCTS use PyTorch's LBFGS optimiser with learning rate 0.1,
500 iterations, and convergence tolerance $10^{-9}$ (gradient) and
$10^{-11}$ (loss change).
Platt Scaling (PS) and Vector Scaling (VS) use Adam with learning rate 0.01
(PS) or 0.05 (VS), weight decay $10^{-4}$, for 2000 epochs.

\paragraph{ECE bins.}
We use $B=15$ equal-width bins in $[0,1]$.  Bins with fewer than 1 example
are excluded from the ECE computation.

\paragraph{MCTS sampling.}
We use $S=50$ annotation samples per calibration example, drawn with a fixed
random seed (42).  Sensitivity to $S$ is negligible for $S\ge 20$.

\paragraph{Compute.}
Fine-tuning runs for approximately 20 minutes on a single NVIDIA A100 GPU.
All calibration methods run in under 60 seconds on CPU after logits are cached.

